  "title": "MySQL: Add tree item for each field in binary protocol",
  "description": "In the binary protocol that is used with prepared statements it wasn't clear which fields in the tree belonged to which field/column in the result. This was especially the case with datetime/timestamp results.\n\nCode:\n```python\n#!/bin/python3\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport mysql.connector\n\nc = mysql.connector.connect(\n    host='127.0.0.1',\n    user='root',\n    database='test',\n    ssl_disabled=True\n)\n\ncur = c.cursor(prepared=True)\n\ncur.execute(\"DROP TABLE IF EXISTS t1\");\ncur.execute(\"\"\"CREATE TABLE t1 (\nid INT PRIMARY KEY,\nt1 timestamp,\nt2 timestamp(6),\nd1 datetime,\nd2 datetime(6),\nj JSON,\nb1 BIT,\nb2 BINARY(25),\ni1 tinyint,\ni2 smallint,\ni3 mediumint,\ni4 int,\ni5 bigint,\ny year,\nd decimal(10,2),\ne ENUM('Y','N'),\ng GEOMETRY)\"\"\")\ncur.execute(\"\"\"INSERT INTO t1 VALUES(\n1,\nNOW(),\nNOW(6),\nNOW(),\nNOW(6),\n'{\"a\": [1,2,3]}',\n1,\n0x000000000101000000000000000000F03F0000000000000040,\n1,\n2,\n3,\n4,\n5,\n2024,\n1.2,\n'Y',\nST_GeomFromText('POINT(1 2)')\n)\"\"\")\n\ncur.execute('TABLE t1');\nfor r in cur:\n    print(r, \"\\n\")\n\nc.commit()\ncur.close()\n\nc.close()\n```\n\nCapture:\n[mysql_ps_datetime_timestamp.pcapng](/uploads/a8434326ded2e62e1b32943252a1f74e/mysql_ps_datetime_timestamp.pcapng)\n\nExample output with this PR:\n\n![image](/uploads/8f97a2354958089e4f2d6cde999132ee/image.png)\n\nExample without this PR:\n\n![image](/uploads/ebd64a8820c75e4c9e63e5914cf48870/image.png)\n\nQuestions for reviewers:\n- This sets the `end` in the call to `proto_tree_add_subtree()` to `-1`, which might not be ok.\n- Another option would be to have datetime/timestamp use a single item instead of multiple.\n- For strings etc. the length is put into an item in the tree. However this is kinda duplicating what's on the status line (screenshot below shows `16` twice). This is less confusing than the issue with datetime/timestamp, but also causing multiple items per column/field.\n\n![image](/uploads/5b6d94e4d9606d176800fc24d79d99cb/image.png)",
